text1:
The Kazimierz class was the first spacecraft class accepted into service within the Polaris Treaty Alliance Exoatmospheric Forces.  Initially designed by Smok Sysdyne in a bid for a Domain navy contract, one that would end up yielding the Champion Class.  Considered too experimental, and with a notable lack of firepower, the design would never- // WARNING  -the revolt of the PTA, the design would be praised within the Exoatmospheric Forces.  Its unique repair drone microforges allow for rapid sorties to be conducted back to back.  These forges would soon be found in all PTA designs. // NON-TRIOS DATASTREAM DETECTED
// TRIOS RESETING DATASTREAM PER USER AGREEMENT F1815-9.0... 

Most captains see the Kazimierz as a flying death trap due to the lack of internal structure.  However in exchange for this lack of structural stability, the Kazimierz gains unparalleled repair ability which allows for all aspects of the hull to be repaired mid combat.  The internal repair drones consume a mountain of preformulated stock to repair the hull, resulting in the Kazimierz’s peak performance diminishing quickly within combat.  The lack of internal structure solves this issue by letting crews fit mountains of feedstock within the Kazimierz, lending surprising longevity within combat.  Enterprising captains can even increase the performance of the repair drones, as long as they also increase the available supply of feedstock.

Designed during the Early Rebellion period, the PTA commissioned Smok Sysdyne to build a capable frontline spacecraft.  The results of phase skimmer experiments allowed for a locally producible variant of a phase skimmer device to be installed. With a large front-facing weapon roster, the Hyacinth was the tip of the Exoatmospheric Forces spear which drove the Domain out of PTA territory.- // NON-TRIOS DATASTREAM DETECTED
// TRIOS RESETING DATASTREAM PER USER AGREEMENT F1815-9.0... 

Despite most captains' qualms with integrating a phase skimmer into a ship of this size, the integrated phase flicker is even more stable and easily repaired than a phase skimmer.  Curious Commonwealth technology aside, the Hyacinth is largely reliant on its heavy weapons and armor profile to keep threats away from its vulnerable rear.

After several battles against Domain Fleets which notoriously favored the decisive battle doctrine, design requirements for a spacecraft capable of screening the Kazimierz whilst also dealing some damage to larger craft were put forth.-  //WARNING -core backbone to most PTA fleets- //WARNING -from New Krakow to Rozonygrod, and even Kaimas- //WARNING - will never surrender, not until we are free from the atrocities of the Domain - // NON-TRIOS DATA STREAM DETECTED
// TRIOS RESETING DATASTREAM PER USER AGREEMENT F1815-9.0... 
//This TriPad is unable to parse the local terminal. 
//Please contact your local TriTachyon dealer for more information.

All Commonwealth ships utilize software packages supposedly developed within an environment devoid of any TriTachyon involvement.  For spacers in the Persean Sector, this means all the computer systems of Commonwealth ships need to be rewritten with conversion software.  Commonwealth shipwrights often do nothing to assist this process. The shipwrights regularly even leave parts of the Commonwealth comnet in the ships data storage caches.  Resulting in the conversion software hitting TriOS hardcoded stops which lock all further progress until the local data cache is cleared.  As one might assume Commonwealth shipwrights have gained a poor reputation amongst spacers.

‘I want that //REDACTED phase cloaking rat ripped from the abyss!  Kowalski! Pull that //REDACTED out now so he can be roasted over a fusion core!’- // NON-TRIOS DATA STREAM DETECTED
// TRIOS RESETING DATASTREAM PER USER AGREEMENT F1815-9.0... 

The Sluagh is a delicate yet fearsome design.  Utilizing weakly acausal principles to overload enemy ships, the tech behind the Sluagh is claimed to be wholly of Commonwealth origin.  Closer inspection suggests it cannot be due to its similarities to TriTachyon designs.  The Sluagh is nonetheless a fast, agile destroyer easily capable of forcing phase ships out of phase and dealing significant damage to them before they can retreat.

Seeking a faster alternative to the Kazimierz which could lead patrol sorties, a new design request was put forth by the PTA-EF.  The bid was taken in stride by a newly founded shipwright, Aitvaras Orbitinis.  Numerous setbacks delayed the project, and while the design criteria was eventually met, the Kaukas never shook its moniker as the “invisible spacecraft”.- 
// NON-TRIOS DATA STREAM DETECTED
// TRIOS RESETING DATASTREAM PER USER AGREEMENT F1815-9.0... 

A fast cruiser best sent on flanking attacks, or to destroy harassing frigates.  Its lackluster weapons profile heavily limits its effectiveness against larger ships.  Its speed paired with the inbuilt repair drone microforges allows the Kaukas to survive all but the most intense pressure.

The first spacecraft designed by Dullahan Shipyards, originally meant for frontline mining, now refined into a- //Warning -with the ability to act as support to other spacecraft with fightercraft and missiles alike, The Oillipheist is major threat to any battle lines if left undisturbed.- //WARNING -for enterprising captains looking to bulk up their operations, the Oillipheist is a true multi-role craft built for every occasion!- // NON-TRIOS DATASTREAM DETECTED
// TRIOS RESETING DATASTREAM PER USER AGREEMENT F1815-9.0... 

A strange ship, the Oillipheist class at first glance would seem to be more a transport ship than combat ship.  Yet the Oillipheist is the premier Commonwealth carrier, and it is due to its perfect ability to carry frigates within its vast and expansive bulk.  Most Oillipheist in service within the Commonwealth Exoatmospheric Forces are equipped with dedicated nanoforges programmed to build and repair frigate sized vessels.

Although lacking the same presence as her sister class, the Rusalka trades size and power for cost and efficiency.  Utilizing state of- //WARNING -On today’s episode, will the TriTachyon spy be uncovered? Or will yet more crim- //WARNING -technology to compact as many of the crafts core systems into as small of a space as possible, the Rusalka affords a truly Multi-role craft to any fleet who purchases her.  Contact the Agropelter Shipyards now for a special offer!-  // NON-TRIOS DATA STREAM DETECTED
// TRIOS RESETING DATASTREAM PER USER AGREEMENT F1815-9.0... 

The Rusalka is best described by the old adage, a jack of all trades but a master of none.  Able to carry noteworthy amounts of cargo and fuel for a ship of its size, and with a fighter hangar, the Rusalka is able to hold its own in hauling and combat.  Yet the Rusalka’s lackluster weapons profile, poor hull integrity, and low cargo capacity compared to dedicated haulers precludes it from performing well as either a combat ship or transport.

//WARNING -the defeat at Kaimas and destruction of the 5th Battlegroup, the PTA requested a new capital class spacecraft to replace the lost number of Conquest Class’ within the Exoatmospheric Forces.- //WARNING -long backlogs, Smok Sysdyne answered the request.- //WARNING -after Jadwiga and her crew, the design would soon be sent to all reaches of the Polaris Sector.- // NON-TRIOS DATASTREAM DETECTED
// TRIOS RESSETING DATASTREAM PER USER AGREEMENT F1815-9.0... 

Heavy modular slabs of armor fitted with unique sets of nodes clutter the hull, able to act as an emp emitter and a damper field projector.  With a brutal weapons profile, fighter pilots are advised to avoid the Jadwiga at all costs.  The Jadwiga’s strong engines mean that Frigate captains are also discouraged from getting too close, lest the Jadwiga’s emp emitter fry your entire ship.   Commonwealth shipwrights often remark that dual emitter-damper nodes were fitted onto the Kazimierz  and Kilian after the design was proven on the Jadwiga.

He nears the goal, but can he score? -//WARNING-  AND THATS A SCORE!- //WARNING- you want to put your chicken or chicken analogue in the oven, and make sure to season it with Miezko brand seasoning! Now- //WARNING- want to see how i live in my log cabin on Zimowia? Stay- //WARNING- Enjoy the relaxing sounds of night-stalkers outside of Ancathair on Ivernia!- // NON-TRIOS DATASTREAM DETECTED
// TRIOS RESSETING DATASTREAM PER USER AGREEMENT F1815-9.0…

The Cailleach Class is a large bulk transport ship which was originally meant as a purely military logistic ship.  Current conditions within the Persean sector have given it heightened relevance however, and it is a prized jewel for many independent hauling operations.  Its overwhelming cost to purchase and operate does limit its adoption amongst independent fleet captains.  Least not due to the utter insanity that is the Cailleach data systems, which have caused many operation crew chiefs to be broken to tears over.

Can the contestants survive 10 days in the wilds of Ivernia? Keep- //Warning -are the recent elections in New Gdansk rigged? Is this a case of Hegemony backed Interference, or- //Warning -Built well before the war, the Pelczar Class is one of the first spacecrafts built by Smok Sysdyne, and has seen over a century of dutiful service.  Simplicity in design, and with a focus on reliability, the Pelczar will see you through the death of the universe.- // NON-TRIOS DATA STREAM DETECTED
// TRIOS RESETING DATASTREAM PER USER AGREEMENT F1815-9.0...   

A large ship for a destroyer, the Peclzar’ design was clearly militarized to support military logistics operations at some point.  This, combined with its sizable cargo and fuel holds, allows the Pelczar to see common usage within the Persean Sector as an effective and fast bulk transport.  At the cost of higher operating costs due to its large size.

The Domain, they’re everywhere! We’re surrounded!- //WARNING -Focus up! Your backups here now, just hold them off as we get into- //WARNING -An entire constellation of Faillinis Classes! You heard the man, prep for combat, we’re not going down without a fight today!- //WARNING -pride of Dullahan Shipyards, the Failinis Class assault platform is a deadly spacecraft which had an unmistakable presence over the entire PTA-Domain frontlines.  Wherever the Failinis was, the PTA advanced tremendously.  The only downside of the class was its cost, as no corners were cut on its design, leading to a more arduous build process whilst granting higher safety and comfort for its crew. -// NON-TRIOS DATASTREAM DETECTED
// TRIOS RESETING DATASTREAM PER USER AGREEMENT F1815-9.0... 

The amount of frontal firepower possessed by the Failinis is more than sufficient to atomize any wayward frigate or destroyer that ends up in its sights.  If the Failinis assault the flanks of an enemy frontline, it will often collapse unless swift action is taken to counter the Failinis.  The Failinis can also effectively open holes within a battleline should a lighter ship get too aggressive.  Lacking a shield, the Failinis is vulnerable to enemy fire should it stay in combat long enough for its armor to get depleted.
